  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39486894",
      "title": "React Query: What & Why?",
      "sourceHash": "2bb8a76e57ed65392d2a626c8efa2039990cddfb5b3548f5f0dbef8d5ceec3e2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.39,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "So before we'll start using Tanstack Query",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 4.92,
          "en": "in this project here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.92,
          "end": 6.75,
          "en": "let's make sure we all understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 9.15,
          "en": "what exactly Tanstack Query is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.15,
          "end": 12.12,
          "en": "and why you might want to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.12,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "And I already mentioned it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 16.62,
          "en": "in the first video of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.62,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "Tanstack Query is a library that helps you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 23.94,
          "en": "with sending HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 27.63,
          "en": "and keeping your frontend user interface in sync",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.63,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "with your backend data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 31.113,
          "en": "That's the core idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.01,
          "end": 34.26,
          "en": "And it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.26,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "that you don't need Tanstack Query to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 39.99,
          "en": "You could do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 44.28,
          "en": "with useEffect and the fetch function, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "That's how you learned to do it earlier in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 51.603,
          "en": "and using this approach is also fine in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "But Tanstack Query can vastly simplify your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "and therefore also your life as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "especially also because it comes with many built in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 67.41,
          "en": "more advanced features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.41,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "which might be needed by more complex React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 73.8,
          "en": "and which are relatively difficult",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.8,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "and challenging to build on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "Now, if we dive into this starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 80.4,
          "en": "I prepared for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 82.92,
          "en": "and there in the src components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.92,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "and then the Events folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 89.40299999999999,
          "en": "you'll find a New Events section component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.42,
          "end": 92.85,
          "en": "And in this component file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 96.66,
          "en": "you will find the useEffect hook being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.66,
          "end": 98.97,
          "en": "to then in the end contain some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.97,
          "end": 102.27000000000001,
          "en": "that will send an HTTP request to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.27000000000001,
          "end": 104.253,
          "en": "and fetch some events data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.69,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "And you'll see that in there we're managing some state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "the data, which we'll eventually have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "a possible error we might be facing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 119.63,
          "en": "and a is loading state to update the UI accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 121.68,
          "en": "So that we show a loading indicator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.68,
          "end": 124.08,
          "en": "whilst we're still waiting for the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.08,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "That we show an error block if we got an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 132.483,
          "en": "or that we output that list of events if we got the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.59,
          "end": 136.53,
          "en": "And here I'm just using a custom event item component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.53,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "which the end simply is responsible for outputting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 141.03300000000002,
          "en": "these items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 146.49,
          "en": "So that's what we're doing here in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.49,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "And what we're doing here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 151.07999999999998,
          "en": "does not need any third party library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 153.78,
          "en": "because we're using features like useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.78,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "and useEffect that are built into React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 159.753,
          "en": "and the fetch function that's built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.95,
          "end": 163.82999999999998,
          "en": "But whilst this approach here works fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.82999999999998,
          "end": 167.04,
          "en": "and as mentioned is fine to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.04,
          "end": 170.013,
          "en": "it has a couple of potential flaws.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 173.91,
          "en": "For example, it's quite a lot of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.91,
          "end": 176.22,
          "en": "that we have to write here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.22,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "We have to write all this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 183.51,
          "en": "in the useEffect hook to make sure that we fetch the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.51,
          "end": 187.44,
          "en": "and then trigger and set our different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.44,
          "end": 189.6,
          "en": "We have to manage all these states,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.6,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "and we have to do that, basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 196.713,
          "en": "in every component that wants to send HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.67000000000002,
          "end": 201.15,
          "en": "Now to be fair, we could simplify this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.15,
          "end": 204.99,
          "en": "and reuse code by building a custom hook, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.99,
          "end": 209.7,
          "en": "We could build a custom use HTTP hook for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.7,
          "end": 213.51,
          "en": "that in the end contains this code and can then be reused.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "And that's also something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 217.68,
          "en": "about which you learned earlier in the course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.68,
          "end": 220.35,
          "en": "how you can build custom hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "But even if we would build such a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 226.41,
          "en": "this code would still have some problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.41,
          "end": 229.53,
          "en": "or missing features to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.53,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "For example, one feature we might want in this app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "but which we don't have yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 238.44,
          "en": "is that if I'm on this website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.44,
          "end": 242.52,
          "en": "and I then switch to a different tab to do something there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 245.82,
          "en": "and I then come back to this website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 249.48,
          "en": "I might want to trigger a refetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.48,
          "end": 253.29,
          "en": "so that behind the scenes we're fetching new data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 254.97,
          "en": "and we're updating the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.97,
          "end": 256.92,
          "en": "if we found out that the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.92,
          "end": 259.983,
          "en": "we're currently displaying is outdated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.97,
          "end": 263.94,
          "en": "Now, out of the box with the code I have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.94,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "we don't have that behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.92,
          "en": "And it would take us quite a bit of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.92,
          "end": 272.103,
          "en": "to write to implement this behavior in a good way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.06,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "Another feature we might want in this app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 278.64,
          "en": "could be caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.64,
          "end": 282.42,
          "en": "so that the data once fetched is cached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 284.55,
          "en": "stored in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.55,
          "end": 289.17,
          "en": "and we can then reuse that data if we need it again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.17,
          "end": 290.52,
          "en": "So that for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.52,
          "end": 294.12,
          "en": "if I go to a different page, the View Details page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 294.12,
          "end": 295.71,
          "en": "which currently doesn't work yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 295.71,
          "end": 299.07,
          "en": "but we'll make it work throughout this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 299.07,
          "end": 301.59,
          "en": "and I then go back to view all events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 301.59,
          "end": 304.62,
          "en": "we don't have to refetch all that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 304.62,
          "end": 308.67,
          "en": "but instead we maybe use the data we already have in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.67,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "and fetch updated data behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 315.57,
          "en": "It's subtle, small features like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.57,
          "end": 318.18,
          "en": "which can make an application much better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.18,
          "end": 320.79,
          "en": "and much more user-friendly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 320.79,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "And building all these things from scratch on your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 326.46,
          "en": "and getting those things right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 326.46,
          "end": 329.73,
          "en": "is definitely challenging and can be difficult.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.73,
          "end": 333.69,
          "en": "And that's where Tanstack Query comes into play",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.69,
          "end": 335.79,
          "en": "because with this library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "we'll not just be able to get rid of a bunch of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "like this state management here and some other code as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 346.56,
          "en": "but we'll also get some advanced features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.56,
          "end": 349.77,
          "en": "like caching behind the scenes, data fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 349.77,
          "end": 352.74,
          "en": "and all those things I just described",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 352.74,
          "end": 355.08,
          "en": "to make our app better and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.08,
          "end": 357.663,
          "en": "let's now get started with Tanstack Query.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}